quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  7,82,But the answer of his people was none other than to say: ‘Expel them from your town. They are a people who seek to keep themselves pure and chaste.’
  7,83,So We saved him (Lot) and his family (and his followers)—except his wife; she was among those who stayed behind.
  7,84,Then We poured upon them a rain (of stones). So observe how (disastrous) was the end of the evildoers!
  7,85,"And to the people of Madyan ([Midian], We sent) their (fellow) brother Shu‘ayb. He said: ‘O my people! Worship Allah! You have no god besides Him. A clear proof has surely come to you from your Lord. So observe fully the measure and the balance, and do not undervalue the goods of the people. And do not cause corruption in the land after it has been set in order. That is better for you if you are (true) believers."
  7,86,"And do not lie in ambush on every path, frightening and hindering those who believe in Him from the way of Allah, seeking to make it crooked. And remember when you were few, and then He multiplied you. And observe how (disastrous) was the end of the corruptors."
  7,87,"If a group among you have believed in what I have been sent with, and another group have not believed, then be patient till Allah judges between us, and He is the best of judges.’"
